export abstract anchor FactorySessions:
    liveness:
        Each adapter declares a discovery capability: token, launch-request
        lookup, reference-only, or unsupported. The declaration is recorded and
        defaults to unsupported. Token discovery injects a durable attempt token
        at launch; matching is exact. Launch-request lookup resolves a retained
        launch identifier and returns not-found only from that retained record,
        never from a timeout, an empty listing, or a failed probe.
        Reference-only relies on a durable session reference plus native status
        or a side-effect-free attach check. Absence, a failed probe, a timeout,
        a client disconnect, and zero token matches are unknown, not not-found
        or ended. A direct lookup by a retained session reference that returns
        gone or not-found is terminal evidence. Launch rejection, queue expiry,
        and cancellation before start are launch outcomes, not session
        evidence. A launcher-process exit is not session evidence unless the
        adapter establishes that the launcher is the session.
        An attempt epoch is assigned before launch from the persisted attempt
        and launch request identifier. Each session carries its own epoch in a
        per-source signal history. Terminal evidence applies only to its epoch,
        so identifier reuse cannot close a newer session.
        A session lease is committed before dispatch and claimed by exactly one
        session identity at adoption. The adapter refuses to launch a second
        session under a claimed lease. Every external effect checks the lease
        epoch. Each session gets a separate worktree before it may write; an
        orphan never shares the owner's worktree.
        Liveness is alive, ended, or unknown, with a timestamp per signal.
        Newer positive terminal evidence wins over older alive evidence;
        conflicting fresh signals produce unknown. Terminal evidence does not
        decay. A signal older than its freshness window becomes unknown, except
        terminal evidence.
        Heartbeat is emitted by the adapter where the harness exposes it.
        Agent-reported heartbeat updates activity only, never liveness. Liveness
        last-signal time and activity last-progress time are separate fields.
        Ended requires positive evidence: native ended or terminated status,
        process exit, or a completed stop protocol. A client disconnect is not
        evidence. Attach probes are side-effect-free and only establish that a
        session exists.
        Multiple exact-token sessions make the attempt unknown, freeze each
        session's worktree, pause dependent dispatch, and require an
        authoritative owner. Ownership is claimed by exactly one session at
        adoption under the session lease; other sessions become orphaned and
        are never silently adopted. A non-owner result is preserved as evidence
        and becomes admissible only after the owner is terminal or abandoned,
        the owner epoch is fenced, and the result is re-based and assessed.
        Unknown liveness preserves the session reference and blocks replacement.
        For token and lookup variants, a resolution deadline defaults to 30
        minutes per cause. At the deadline the attempt becomes unresolved, not
        interrupted: it keeps a quarantine concurrency slot and its budget
        reservation floor, its worktree is frozen, and escalation offers wait,
        investigate, stop, or authorized replacement. With reference-only
        discovery, a crash between launch and persistence becomes unresolved at
        the deadline under the same rules. No retry or replacement may launch
        while unresolved.
        An unresolved session can be stopped through its per-session stop
        handle by code for budget, policy, or duplicate containment, or by the
        engineer. A confirmed stop transitions the attempt from unresolved to
        interrupted with an audited terminal-to-terminal transition. An
        unconfirmed stop leaves it unresolved and escalates.
        An account-wide aggregate of unresolved exposure, measured in estimated
        currency and usage units rather than attempt count, stops new launches
        on that account and escalates. Other accounts and unrelated orders
        continue.
        Adapter errors are classified as auth, config, wiring, outage, rate
        limit, or liveness. Auth, config, and wiring route to repair; outage and
        non-allowance rate limits use retry policy; exhausted allowance is a
        budget blocker; liveness is reserved for genuine indeterminacy. Process
        exits map to completed with result, failed, or interrupted by exit
        cause.
